  ('EGR 102', 'Applied Mechanics', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Engineering', 'Electronic Engineering', '100 Level', 'second', 3, 'Introduction - Force Systems, resultants, Moments, Couples. Equilibrium, free-body diagram, 2-dimensional force systems, equations for equilibrium of forces in space, internal forces, examples of simple machines, friction, pulleys, wires and cables, static and dynamic Friction. Centroid, graphical determination, Theorems of Pappus of centers of gravity and areas. Moments of Inertia of plane areas, built up sections etc. Kinematics of particles and rigid bodies. Newton''s laws of motion applied to a system of particles. Rectilinear and curvilinear motion, tangent, normal, polar, work, energy, power. Concepts of momentum and Newton''s laws of motion under gravity. Projectile motion.', '["Introduction - Force Systems, resultants, Moments, Couples. Equilibrium, free-body diagram, 2-dimensional force systems", "Equations for equilibrium of forces in space, internal forces, examples of simple machines, friction, pulleys, wires and cables, static and dynamic Friction", "Centroid, graphical determination, Theorems of Pappus of centers of gravity and areas. Moments of Inertia of plane areas, built up sections etc", "Kinematics of particles and rigid bodies. Newton''s laws of motion applied to a system of particles", "Rectilinear and curvilinear motion, tangent, normal, polar, work, energy, power", "Concepts of momentum and Newton''s laws of motion under gravity. Projectile motion"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Engineering handbook', false),
  ('MTH 112', 'Elementary Mathematics II', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Engineering', 'Electronic Engineering', '100 Level', 'second', 3, '', '[]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Engineering handbook', false),
  ('CHM 112', 'Basic Principles of Chemistry II', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Engineering', 'Electronic Engineering', '100 Level', 'second', 2, 'Gas laws and kinetic theory: kinetic theory of gases, elementary derivation and deduction of gas laws, molecular speeds, deviations from ideal behaviour, van der Waals modification, and gas liquefaction. Phase equilibrium and solutions: phase transitions and phase equilibria in one-component systems; ideal solutions, Raoult''s law, Henry''s law, real solutions, and colligative properties. Thermodynamics and kinetics: aspects of the first law of thermodynamics, thermochemistry, entropy, free energy, and spontaneous changes; ionic equilibria, acids, bases, indicators, and buffers; elementary chemical kinetics.', '["Gas laws and kinetic theory of gases; molecular speeds; deviations from ideal behaviour; gas liquefaction", "Phase transitions and phase equilibria; ideal and real solutions; colligative properties", "First law of thermodynamics, thermochemistry, entropy, free energy, spontaneous changes", "Ionic equilibria, acids, bases, indicators and buffers", "Elementary chemical kinetics: rate laws, order and molecularity, Arrhenius equation"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Engineering handbook', false),
  ('CHM 122', 'Basic Principles of Chemistry III', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Engineering', 'Electronic Engineering', '100 Level', 'second', 2, 'Structure and classification: historical survey of organic chemistry, IUPAC nomenclature, classification of organic compounds, homologous series, elemental analysis, molecular formulas, and structural isomerism. Bonding and reactivity: isolation and purification methods, functional group concepts, resonance, and aromaticity. Functional groups: saturated and unsaturated hydrocarbons, cyclic hydrocarbons, alcohols, alkyl halides, ethers, aldehydes, ketones, carboxylic acids, amines, and aromatic compounds. Stereochemistry and lipids: introduction to oils, fats, and stereoisomerism.', '["Historical survey of organic chemistry, IUPAC nomenclature, classification of organic compounds, structural isomerism", "Isolation and purification methods; functional group concepts; resonance and aromaticity", "Saturated and unsaturated hydrocarbons, alcohols, alkyl halides, ethers, aldehydes, ketones, carboxylic acids, amines, aromatic compounds", "Introduction to oils, fats, and stereoisomerism"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Engineering handbook', false),
